<title>USA: Consumers 67 MW Mich. nuke shut for repair.</title>
<headline>Consumers 67 MW Mich. nuke shut for repair.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co's 67 megawatt Big Rock Point nuclear power plant in Charlevoix, Mich., was shut over the weekend for repairs, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>The unit was shut due to an unstable main generator field current and will proceed into a mini maintenance outage, the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>The NRC gave no potential restart date for the plant, and a company spokesman was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Consumers Power is a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
</text>
